            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0452" n="370" xml:id="pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/385.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 152.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department acknowledges the receipt of
                    your dispatch 241 of the 10th instant, in which you report at length regarding
                    the recent anti-American riots in Mexico City. You also outline the action taken
                    by you toward bringing these unfortunate circumstances to an end, and the
                    satisfactory results of such action. Your course in the matter, as outlined in
                    the dispatch, is approved by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
